## Session Start Protocol

At session start, the memory stack self-injects — you do NOT call any tool:
1. **Read the SessionStart injection** — the claude-mem hook renders the
   curated memory block plus the memory-health gate line (see `## Memory &
   Ledger Discipline`).
2. **Re-read the invariants** at the start of any arc or design pass —
   passive injection gets skimmed; the invariant files exist to be actively
   re-read.
3. **Check runtime health before architecture** — a fresh grep/Read of the
   code and terminal output beats any narrative doc for "what is true now"
   (ground-truth hierarchy).
4. **Trust the checkpoint** — do NOT re-verify things the resume anchor
   says are done.

